      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَادِيَةٌ</span></b>  <i>A cloud that rises</i> (S, K) <i>in the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">صَبَاح</span> (S)
or <i>in the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غُدْوَة</span> (K) [i. e. <i>in the first part of the
day</i>]: or <i>a rain of the</i> [<i>period of the morning
called</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَدَاة</span>: (K, TA:) thus says Lh: the pl. is
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">غَوَادٍ</span>. (TA.) [See a verse in the Ham p. 429.]

